{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_client.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:00:57.101344Z","id":"406b9f584ec83ba6ec24345a46b0f6628fa7d475577e7cbe35f8b47e2a2083af","body":{"detail":"clax_embed_subscribe (crates/clax-embed/include/clax_embed.h) takes only a handle and a port, so a shell document's subscribe {lastEventId} (spec 2026-10-19 §2.4, §5.2) cannot resume the core's stream; record 9a8a7d42 tracks the core's half on crates/clax-embed/src/events.rs:30. When the ABI gains it, CoreLib.subscribe takes the ID and this method passes it instead of throwing; apps/clax_app/test/core/core_client_test.dart 'a resume point is refused until the C functions carry one' then changes to assert it reaches the lib.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":200},"end":{"line":214},"content_hash":"1101aeff0dfd4a60f1d6d6903a0026ed090b5b020862eb639d0f1e4a60de6741"},"summary":"CoreClient.subscribe throws UnsupportedError for a non-null lastEventId: the C ABI has no resume point yet","tags":["revisit:clax_embed_subscribe takes a resume point","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_client.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:07:12.837435Z","id":"070410dab9b82226a854e65906db38b44028076544008a6a41fcf17e4a6abf6a","body":{"detail":"CoreClient.call answers status 0 core_failed for handle 0, and status 0 core_closed after close, for clax_embed_call's 1, and for calls still pending at CoreClosed (CoreResponse.unanswered, apps/clax_app/lib/core/frame.dart:81-91). The core answers the same conditions as real frames: 503 core_failed for a handle whose open failed (crates/clax-embed/src/lib.rs:209), 503 core_closed for a call admitted while it drains or cut at the drain's end (crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs:566-583). An attached client (the worker isolate of Task 25) never sees the opener's close, so during one close it gets 503 core_closed for calls the drain refuses, then status 0 core_closed once ffi_close has forgotten the handle. Domain code branches on the status: apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart:1094-1096 turns status 0 into ChangeInterrupted (retry) and any other error into ChangeFailed(answered: true), and lib/clax/stream.dart:315 treats both as transient. So the same 'the core closed' is either a retry or a failure the person sees, depending on which side noticed it. The client also fails in three other ways: an ArgumentError for clax_embed_call's 2, a FormatException for a frame it cannot decode, and a call left pending forever when a message is shorter than 8 bytes. CoreResponse means both 'a frame the core sent' and 'something the client made up', and only the number 0 tells them apart.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":174},"end":{"line":198},"content_hash":"a0f26cea8c18daf0ecb75b34319735ad362f2e84393537d1db2523481b78f72b"},"suggested_fix":"Make CoreCalls.call return a sealed outcome: CoreAnswered(CoreResponse) | CoreUnanswered(code: core_failed | core_closed, message). CoreClient folds the core's own 503 core_failed/core_closed frames into CoreUnanswered, so either side's notice reads the same. CoreTransport (Task 13) maps CoreUnanswered to ClaxApiError(status: 0, code), which is spec section 6's 'no answer came' contract for ClaxTransport.send. Domain code then keeps one meaning for status 0, and CoreResponse holds only frames the core actually sent. The plan's Task 12 Step 2 ('close completes pending calls with status 0 core_closed') and Task 13's CoreTransport note change with it.","summary":"One condition, two shapes: CoreClient answers a closed or failed core with a made-up status 0, while the core answers the same condition itself with 503 core_closed / core_failed, and the agent loop treats those two shapes differently","tags":["review","spec:6","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_client.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:07:12.837720Z","id":"5a16d6dcb64d9093e500bb9fd75a2f1bdd6c8c64bebffdcad84d0411f60590e0","body":{"detail":"The core counts a call in flight only while answer() runs (crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs:558, _counted dropped when answer returns). It posts the response bytes later, in ffi_call's spawned task, after call_owned returns (crates/clax-embed/src/lib.rs:217-230). Embed::close waits for the count to reach 0 (core.rs:370), stops the core and emits Closed (core.rs:382), and nothing orders that emit after the post. If closed arrives first, CoreClient._finish completes the still-pending call with status 0 core_closed and closes _answers, and the real answer (say, 200 to a publish that committed) is dropped. The agent loop treats status 0 as interrupted and retries (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart:1094), so the write can happen twice. The test 'lets calls in flight drain, then answers the rest core_closed' (apps/clax_app/test/core/core_client_test.dart:150-180) shows a late answer after closed being dropped, as designed. The window is small (core.stop and the store close run in between), but nothing rules it out.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":276},"end":{"line":293},"content_hash":"e10cb30c4c55d1d0849ec15734364e798f05a307c7e3eefca6ef49e4c8be266c"},"suggested_fix":"Have the core keep a call counted until its answer is posted: take the InFlight guard in ffi_call's task around call_owned and post_bytes, or post from inside answer(). Then every drained call's answer reaches the isolate before closed, and _finish's core_closed covers only calls the core never took. Add a Rust test where close races a call whose post is slowed, and check that closed comes after the answer.","summary":"The core can post closed before the answer of a call it drained, and _finish then answers that call core_closed: a committed write reads as unanswered","tags":["review","spec:2.2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_client.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:07:12.837891Z","id":"5aa7e294b3c44066384710d318cbe140cb6b8fc8c8722910cda3c6b5d4391dc2","body":{"detail":"Embed::open refuses a home this process already holds (crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs:224, OpenError::HomeInUse), and ffi_open answers 0 for it (crates/clax-embed/src/lib.rs:171). The old handle lived only in the dead isolate's memory, and the C ABI has no way to find or close a core by its home. After a hot restart of `just dev` / `flutter run`, CoreClient.open shows CoreFailed home_in_use ('Clax is already open on <home> in this app.'). The orphaned core still holds core.lock and the store, and it posts open events to a port that is gone. Also, the handle-0 path posts CoreFailed but leaves _stateOut and _answers open until close() is called, so `states` is not done after the failure.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":123},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"d00723244f5f7a7868c442d48a6f352bfdf2656a40ba6fa5e8c643e98f2113ed"},"suggested_fix":"Let clax_embed_open adopt the open core for the same home in the same process: give back its handle and move its open-event port to the new port, posting ready (or the current phase) there. Or add a close-by-home that the new isolate calls before it opens. Either way, test it in core_real_test by opening twice without closing.","summary":"A UI isolate that restarts without close (a Flutter hot restart, or an engine that restarts its root isolate) cannot open the core again: open answers handle 0 home_in_use until the process exits","tags":["review","spec:2.5","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/ffi.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:07:12.838307Z","id":"53cfbdaa03cab709e9f51610de5d57da330a711a670a898f61723a67395f58b7","body":{"detail":"CoreRequest.encode copies the body into a new frame (apps/clax_app/lib/core/frame.dart:65-70). _lent copies the whole frame into malloc memory (ffi.dart:103-111), and clax_embed_call copies it once more (crates/clax-embed/src/lib.rs, Bytes::copy_from_slice in ffi_call). For a publish near PUBLISH_BODY_LIMIT (96 MiB, spec section 2.3) that is about 384 MiB alive at once on a phone, and two of those copies run on the calling isolate's thread. Spec section 2.3 counts only the core's copies.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":91},"end":{"line":112},"content_hash":"98d029a7a21d4ae5a8556c87d46ed60fcae2c86bf87284279da27587fa4235a8"},"suggested_fix":"Encode the frame straight into the malloc'd buffer (write the magic, the length, the head and the body into p.asTypedList), so Dart makes one native copy and no intermediate frame. Keep CoreRequest.encode for tests and FakeCoreLib.","summary":"A large request is held four times at its peak: the caller's body, the frame, the malloc copy and the core's copy, all copied synchronously on the calling isolate","tags":["review","spec:2.3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/ffi.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:07:12.838434Z","id":"38b1ea564a07231c6e9cff153098d7772911d0acd25b6620abb750e3194a4067","body":{"detail":"The choice per platform (Android libclax_embed.so, iOS DynamicLibrary.process(), macOS CLAX_EMBED_LIB or <bundle>/Contents/Frameworks/libclax_embed.dylib) runs only on a device or in the real suite (CLAX_EMBED_LIB is set), so the Android, iOS and bundle paths are never checked. The environment override is read in every build mode, so a shipped macOS app loads whatever dylib the variable names; a hardened runtime ignores DYLD_* variables but not this one, and only library validation stands in the way. On Linux or Windows (a host `flutter test` without the variable), load() opens <exe>/../Frameworks/libclax_embed.dylib and fails with an error naming a macOS path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"486e4ec06ab7cac0223713aa5344bc43a489897c6d5f8b092ff011fa7c57f7ba"},"suggested_fix":"Split out a pure function: `CoreLibSource coreLibSource({required String os, required Map<String, String> env, required String executable, required bool release})`, returning a sealed Open(path) | Process | Unsupported(os). Unit-test it for each platform in frame_test or a new ffi_test, then make load() a two-line interpreter over DynamicLibrary. Read CLAX_EMBED_LIB only when !release (kReleaseMode or bool.fromEnvironment('dart.vm.product')).","summary":"CoreLib.load picks its library inline from Platform, untested; it honours CLAX_EMBED_LIB in release builds; and on other hosts it falls through to the macOS bundle path","tags":["review","spec:6","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/frame.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:07:12.838532Z","id":"959dca61caf6e0dac728169da9812d90761b8361118209af8c468e3db76d99e1","body":{"detail":"CoreResponse.decode catches TypeError but not UnsupportedError: a head whose status is 1e400 decodes to double.infinity, and toInt() throws. _answer (apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_client.dart:235-245) removes the completer before it decodes and catches only FormatException, so that call never completes and the error escapes the RawReceivePort handler. decode also takes any number as a status, including 0 (which the client reserves for 'unanswered') and values outside 100-599. A message shorter than 8 bytes, or one that is not a Uint8List, is dropped silently, so the call it was meant for waits forever. In _Subscription, malformed UTF-8 makes the chunked decoder throw inside the port handler (core_client.dart:319-323), and _isEnd judges each message on its own, though spec section 2.4 allows a block split across messages, so an end block split after 'event: end\\n' would end the stream without its reason. The core sends none of these today. This is about how sturdy the code is, not a live failure.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"da2f3a33b77dd616090e4ca60a788a29d6ae877246ba35a564e7bfea16014dd3"},"suggested_fix":"In decode, require status to be an int in 100-599 and turn any other error (`on Object`) into a FormatException. In _answer, catch Object and complete the call with an error. Decode subscription bytes with allowMalformed: true, and look for the end event on the decoded text, buffered to its blank line, rather than on each raw message. Add a client test that posts a malformed answer frame and a truncated message.","summary":"Malformed input that is not a FormatException leaves a call pending forever or escapes into the isolate's uncaught errors","tags":["review","spec:2.3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_client.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:12:50.465354Z","id":"ea83787131e777ad1ea3e71996d547ad74edb48eca6b5dfb80b466a71c67d5da","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"070410dab9b82226a854e65906db38b44028076544008a6a41fcf17e4a6abf6a","summary":"The owner chose on 2026-10-19: calls return a sealed CoreAnswer, CoreAnswered(CoreResponse) or CoreUnanswered(code); the client folds the core's own 503 core_closed/core_failed into CoreUnanswered, and CoreTransport (plan Task 13) maps CoreUnanswered to ClaxApiError(0, code).","tags":["status:decided","spec:6","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_client.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:12:50.538563Z","id":"00d2eb2c2e9fbec45a14f2b2a7fafbd503ea79f67d0309b4f4c118b49b5ad4e9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2759ff007","summary":"CoreCalls.call returns CoreAnswer (apps/clax_app/lib/core/frame.dart CoreAnswer.of folds the core's 503 core_closed/core_failed); frame_refused and malformed replace the ArgumentError and FormatException; a failed open answers waiting and new calls core_failed. Evidence: bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:core_core_client_test PASSED ('the core's own 503 core_closed and core_failed are unanswered', 'a frame the core refuses goes unanswered as frame_refused', 'an answer that is not a frame goes unanswered as malformed', 'a failed open ends every call, sent or not, as core_failed'); core_core_real_test PASSED.","supersedes":"070410dab9b82226a854e65906db38b44028076544008a6a41fcf17e4a6abf6a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_client.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:12:57.578993Z","id":"9fc3b1a8dd94aa897e409cb0c98b0751e4350e9ffa9cf4b39d4286c40cd7f105","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"406b9f584ec83ba6ec24345a46b0f6628fa7d475577e7cbe35f8b47e2a2083af","summary":"Since 34068b30f CoreClient.subscribe ignores lastEventId instead of throwing: the subscription is a new stream (ready resumed: false) and SseClaxStream resyncs. Still open: when clax_embed_subscribe takes a resume point, CoreLib.subscribe passes it, and core_client_test 'a resume point is ignored until the C functions carry one' changes to assert it reaches the lib.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/ffi.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:13:12.004511Z","id":"929844f0a54206e27836c69e8322e34ad594bdc066308e7e67a786f0ffca38da","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bd48937cf","summary":"CoreRequest.frame() gives a RequestFrame that lendFrame writes once into malloc'd memory; the Dart-side frame copy is gone (CoreLib.call takes the RequestFrame). Evidence: bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:core_ffi_test PASSED ('lends the frame's exact bytes and length in native memory', 70 000-byte body included; 'writes only its own bytes, the body as given'); core_core_real_test PASSED.","supersedes":"53cfbdaa03cab709e9f51610de5d57da330a711a670a898f61723a67395f58b7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/ffi.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:13:12.265387Z","id":"ef23c57409d2c47e37c402361d9a49916b5e654d3534cf2f1c7f8a071f9d414f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3ba25d6ce","summary":"coreLibSource({os, env, executable, release}) is pure and returns CoreLibOpen | CoreLibProcess | CoreLibUnsupported; CLAX_EMBED_LIB is read outside release builds only; Linux/Windows are CoreLibUnsupported with a reason naming the platform and CLAX_EMBED_LIB; CoreLib.load interprets it. Evidence: bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:core_ffi_test PASSED (group coreLibSource: Android .so, iOS process, macOS Contents/Frameworks, release ignores CLAX_EMBED_LIB, Linux/Windows unsupported).","supersedes":"38b1ea564a07231c6e9cff153098d7772911d0acd25b6620abb750e3194a4067","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/frame.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:13:12.542897Z","id":"f195a6a74b61f23b84390ed73f6830bf13212197bdb214ca34a62d6e20895151","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ca4754d56","summary":"decode reads the head by pattern and takes only an integer status 100-599, so every malformed frame is a FormatException and its call is CoreUnanswered malformed; a message without a readable tag is logged; subscriptions buffer to each block's blank line and decode whole blocks, so a split end block keeps its reason and non-UTF-8 ends the subscription with reason malformed. Evidence: bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:core_core_client_test PASSED (group 'malformed input'), core_frame_test PASSED ('bytes that are not a frame are a FormatException').","supersedes":"959dca61caf6e0dac728169da9812d90761b8361118209af8c468e3db76d99e1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_client.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:21:49.606760Z","id":"25ef2c11869342914d9642ef8c9cf15a6a4189c1b3f01f155e9dcac470a6abd0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b18d11505","summary":"Fixed in the core in b18d11505: ffi_call takes an in-flight guard (Embed::count_call) before it spawns the call and drops it after post_bytes, so Embed::close, which waits for the count, posts closed only after each drained answer was posted. Evidence: crates/clax-embed/src/lib.rs tests::a_call_is_counted_until_its_answer_is_posted_so_closed_comes_after_it failed with the guard dropped before the post ('the call was not counted while its answer was posted') and passes; bazelisk test --keep_going //crates/clax-embed:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-store:all //scripts:no_unsafe //scripts:no_unsafe_test //scripts:crate_layers at 817e9401b: 19 tests pass.","supersedes":"5a16d6dcb64d9093e500bb9fd75a2f1bdd6c8c64bebffdcad84d0411f60590e0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_client.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:21:49.673121Z","id":"167308269655a7bba0e9854d734004dc21a2548ff4c7f0be8404f68bf982ec60","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:817e9401b","summary":"Fixed in the core in 817e9401b: clax_embed_open of a home this process holds re-attaches, returning the live core's handle, moving its open events to the new port and posting the latest one there (ready, or where opening has got to); a closing core's home and a non-UTF-8 path answer 0 with failed posted (home_in_use, open_failed). Header and spec §2.2/§2.5 updated. Evidence: lib.rs tests::an_open_of_a_home_this_process_holds_reattaches_to_its_core and an_open_that_answers_0_still_posts_failed (handle 0 and a 60 s timeout before; pass after), ffi.rs a_path_that_is_not_utf8_answers_0_and_a_home_open_already_its_handle; bazelisk test --keep_going //crates/clax-embed:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-store:all //scripts:no_unsafe //scripts:no_unsafe_test //scripts:crate_layers at 817e9401b: 19 tests pass. The Dart side's handle-0 branch is a separate record on core_client.dart.","supersedes":"5aa7e294b3c44066384710d318cbe140cb6b8fc8c8722910cda3c6b5d4391dc2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_client.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:21:49.742240Z","id":"2ba5b1acec8a6dff5850be2c5f36269b12d79b4b4f2cc06987fc74278036b4fb","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-embed/src/lib.rs ffi_open now re-attaches an open of a home this process holds (returns the live handle; the port hears the latest open event), and answers 0 only when that home's core is closing (posts failed home_in_use) or the path is not UTF-8 (posts failed open_failed). CoreClient.open closes the states port at once on 0, so the posted failed is dropped, adds its own CoreFailed('home_in_use', 'Clax is already open on $home in this app.'), and does not close _stateOut, so `states` is not done after the failure (the Dart half of 5aa7e294).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"7effb3ea7c58b3510299277ad819b8cbefac64cde11cd8bfa17d2010eb70333a"},"suggested_fix":"On handle 0, read the failed the core posted (keep the port until it arrives) or word the synthesized failure for a closing core; close _stateOut after the terminal state. A Dart test can open the same home twice without closing and expect the same handle and a second ready.","summary":"On handle 0 the client still reports home_in_use 'Clax is already open on <home> in this app' and leaves states open; since 817e9401b the core answers 0 only for a home whose core is closing or a path that is not UTF-8, and posts failed to the port first","tags":["review","app","embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_transport.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:29:40.925843Z","id":"c6c2084831984a9ef7f8a59fc2a50dda8bd13908bc6f7341bcf4febcc221159d","body":{"detail":"CoreTransport.sse serves only /api/stream with no query, since CoreCalls.subscribe opens only the core's /api/stream subscription and FakeCore.admits / crates/clax-embed core admit refuse /api/events as a held-open route. lib/app.dart:1231 (artifact_deleted) and lib/ui/thread_detail.dart:389 still read HttpClaxApi.events (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/http_api.dart:455-466), so an app switched to HttpClaxApi.over(CoreTransport(...)) would lose those events.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":109},"content_hash":"ac22df09d8c5a4c1421e1aa9d20cb437b54b78a7ed08befaefca4905d43a87a2"},"suggested_fix":"Before the app runs on the core, move those two readers to ClaxStream topics (artifact:<id>, gallery), or drop events() from ClaxApi.","summary":"HttpClaxApi.events (GET /api/events) has no way through CoreTransport: over the core it ends at once with 404 not_in_app","tags":["core","transport","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_client.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:33:06.653977Z","id":"60ecd2713f5f4f2edb94671c8e5f958e590cd6c3bc60620f2fa8ebea28fc142c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8180c2445","summary":"Fixed in 8180c2445: on handle 0 CoreClient.open keeps the states port, reports the CoreFailed the core posted (its code and message), then finishes (states done, ports closed); close() on handle 0 waits for that failed instead of inventing CoreClosed. The re-attach needs no Dart change beyond docs: a nonzero live handle is followed as any open. Evidence: core_client_test 'an open answered 0 reports the core's home_in_use/open_failed, then is done' and 'an open answered 0 waits for the core's failed, even past close' failed before (emitted CoreFailed(home_in_use: Clax is already open on ... in this app.)) and pass; core_real_test 'an open of a home this process holds re-attaches to its core' (second open: same handle, only CoreReady, GET /api/artifacts 200) passes; bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:core_core_client_test //apps/clax_app:core_core_real_test //apps/clax_app:dart_analyze PASSED.","supersedes":"2ba5b1acec8a6dff5850be2c5f36269b12d79b4b4f2cc06987fc74278036b4fb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_transport.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:35:05.875017Z","id":"6619c0905ce1940ff3a77feb24de06377c11f2d8499bea61b8bf2aa29030734c","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-embed/src/events.rs:79-82 ends a ready core's subscription with stream_refused for any non-success status of GET /api/stream, a transient 5xx included. CoreTransport.sse ends the stream with an error on it (core_transport.dart:152-160), and SseClaxStream then stops for good (lib/clax/stream.dart:171-176). reconnectingSse ends only on 400, 403 or 404 and retries the rest with backoff (lib/clax/sse.dart:186-194). The same refusal is a retry on one transport and the end of the app's events on the other.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":151},"end":{"line":161},"content_hash":"32416fab52a49f262cd8a6da79bc346f3442af44e82a3c9ee4224c4a5cf54bd7"},"suggested_fix":"Have the core's end block carry the refusal's status ({\"reason\":\"stream_refused\",\"status\":503}) and end only on 400/403/404, as loopback does; until then, resubscribe after stream_refused with the stream_ended backoff.","summary":"A stream_refused end is final over the core, while loopback retries every refusal but 400, 403 and 404","tags":["review","transport","core","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_transport.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:35:05.875123Z","id":"7c2e2da209bf87c8a68cbb2d93ccd58a2f613686ab93ec50b988b637e981297e","body":{"detail":"Over loopback a timeout aborts the request (lib/clax/transport.dart:122), and the daemon drops the handler with the connection. CoreCalls has no way to cancel a call (lib/core/core_client.dart:85-95), so after the deadline at core_transport.dart:56-65 the core still runs it and its answer is dropped at line 69. For GET /api/sessions/{sid}/feedback (deadline wait + pollSlack, lib/clax/http_api.dart:263-275) the core's take_feedback (crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs:1158) marks the batch delivered and acknowledged, and the app never sees it. The router's own deadlines answer first in normal operation, so this needs a core that is stuck or starved past the Dart deadline.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":55},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"25781e20d1b1f6d8fd88f637409b22e3defaa3cbc9bab27afa4663f216846f80"},"suggested_fix":"Either a cancellable call (a cancel by tag through clax_embed, spec §2.2, dropping the call's future in the core) or a recorded waiver that the core's own deadlines bound every call and the Dart deadline is only a guard.","summary":"A call CoreTransport gives up on keeps running in the core: a timed-out feedback poll can still take a batch whose answer is dropped","tags":["review","core","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_transport.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:35:05.875853Z","id":"7264b29fe9e5e044f0715d1c1e359d67701a3f49fc02ca42bbd819b3f4989e93","body":{"detail":"The topics already carry what the readers need: artifact_deleted is a gallery event (crates/clax-realtime/src/stream.rs Chan::Gallery; web/shell/src/events.ts:9), and thread, comment, thread_resolved, thread_deleted, feedback_state and version are artifact:<aid> events. lib/app.dart _startBundles (1231): subscribe the app-lifetime stream (app.dart:1475) to gallery and give forgetDeleted (lib/bundle/installer.dart:437) a Stream<StreamEvent>. lib/ui/thread_detail.dart:389: take a ClaxStream as InboxScreen does (lib/ui/inbox_screen.dart:104,251), subscribe artifact:<aid> before the first _load (subscribe, then fetch), reload on _eventTypes and on resync and unsubscribed. Then delete ClaxApi.events, ClaxEvent, HttpClaxApi.events and FakeClaxApi.events; ClaxTransport.sse loses its path and query (GET /api/stream is the only stream), and CoreTransport's not_in_app branch (core_transport.dart:101-109) goes with them.","kind":"comment","references":"c6c2084831984a9ef7f8a59fc2a50dda8bd13908bc6f7341bcf4febcc221159d","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":109},"content_hash":"ac22df09d8c5a4c1421e1aa9d20cb437b54b78a7ed08befaefca4905d43a87a2"},"summary":"Move both readers to ClaxStream topics now, so the two transports share one event path, and delete ClaxApi.events","tags":["review","transport","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/core/ffi.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:47:40.258416Z","id":"28727e7a440be80d50ed02e16f4db341ce49ea1987ca02506ce3884e0a7e40d8","body":{"detail":"executable.lastIndexOf('/', macOS - 1) gets a negative start when the path has no slash or only a leading one ('/Clax'), and Dart's lastIndexOf throws RangeError for a negative start, so the pure function the doc describes throws instead of returning a source. For an executable outside an app bundle (a Dart VM running the app's code without CLAX_EMBED_LIB) it returns <grandparent>/Frameworks/libclax_embed.dylib, and CoreLib.load fails in DynamicLibrary.open with a missing-library ArgumentError rather than CoreLibUnsupported's reason naming CLAX_EMBED_LIB. ffi_test.dart's coreLibSource group uses only /Applications/Clax.app/Contents/MacOS/Clax.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":123},"end":{"line":126},"content_hash":"fdef2f1a7c95a5744dbc774777af4f4e049478f072064240f670de184ca10266"},"suggested_fix":"Match the executable against '<bundle>/Contents/MacOS/<name>' and return CoreLibUnsupported with the CLAX_EMBED_LIB hint when it does not; test '/Clax', 'Clax' and '/usr/local/bin/dart'.","summary":"coreLibSource's macOS branch throws RangeError for an executable path with fewer than two slashes, and names a dylib outside any bundle for an executable not in Contents/MacOS","tags":["review","app","ffi","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
